WEBVTT

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.270
There's no going back to those days,

00:00:19.353 --> 00:00:26.819
but I swear that now,
I'll beat out your sorrow

00:00:28.321 --> 00:00:31.073
| may not overcome it unharmed,

00:00:31.157 --> 00:00:35.912
exhaustively marking the footprints

00:00:35.995 --> 00:00:39.916
of the journey to meet you again

00:00:39.999 --> 00:00:45.755
You once taught me that

00:00:45.838 --> 00:00:51.594
the pounding of the heart
is what drives us on

00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:57.600
They haven't taken our future away,

00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:02.271
and knowing that, I can go on

00:01:02.355 --> 00:01:03.564
Just go on

00:01:03.648 --> 00:01:10.404
As long as you smile,
as long as you can sing,

00:01:10.488 --> 00:01:14.575
that becomes everything that I desire

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:15.284
Wow

00:01:15.326 --> 00:01:22.083
The courage you've given me,
the kindness you've shown me,

00:01:22.166 --> 00:01:28.297
gives me the strength
to look forward and walk on

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:37.306
Both of you are well-skilled.
However, that fine skill will prove fatal.

00:01:40.017 --> 00:01:41.477
Ryuo, wait!

00:01:42.687 --> 00:01:43.646
Ryuo!

00:01:45.022 --> 00:01:46.148
What?!

00:01:48.985 --> 00:01:50.945
O-Oh, crap!

00:01:51.988 --> 00:01:53.239
Ryuo!

00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:54.615
Watch out, Doggie!

00:01:59.328 --> 00:02:01.622
Stop! Are you trying to get yourself killed?!

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.961
Stop!!

00:02:08.004 --> 00:02:12.300
Whoal! The Mokona and
the Ryuga have collided!

00:02:17.346 --> 00:02:18.973
Syaoran-kun!

00:02:36.657 --> 00:02:39.910
Doggie, I'm alive because
you slammed your car into mine.

00:02:39.994 --> 00:02:41.912
If you hadn't, right now, I'd be...

00:02:41.996 --> 00:02:42.913
| owe you one.

00:02:42.997 --> 00:02:45.958
Never mind that,
I'm just glad you're not hurt.

00:02:47.001 --> 00:02:50.129
You really are a nice guy, huh?

00:02:51.005 --> 00:02:52.298
Syaoran-kun!

00:02:55.009 --> 00:02:56.302
Princess...

00:02:57.345 --> 00:02:58.304
Right.

00:03:00.848 --> 00:03:03.517
Except for the Wing Egg,
which is in last place,

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:06.228
the other machines have
entered the third checkpoint!

00:03:10.024 --> 00:03:14.028
The last hurdle is an area of
geysers that erupt unpredictably!

00:03:17.656 --> 00:03:20.242
Whoa! The Kuro-tan, a favorite to win,

00:03:20.326 --> 00:03:23.454
forces his way though on his innate power!

00:03:25.331 --> 00:03:28.292
At last, the Wing Egg catches up!

00:03:30.669 --> 00:03:33.964
There's no telling when
the water will come up, huh?

00:03:35.674 --> 00:03:36.967
| can tell.

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:48.479
Oh, the Wing Egg has
moved into second place!

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:03.619
Kuro-pon!

00:04:12.002 --> 00:04:13.587
Kurogane-san!

00:04:13.671 --> 00:04:14.922
Go on!

00:04:15.005 --> 00:04:16.757
But...

00:04:16.841 --> 00:04:19.927
You made up your mind to do this, right?

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.262
Go on.

00:04:21.345 --> 00:04:22.304
Right.

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:39.613
Message for Miss Tomoyo.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:44.910
As of yet, none of the other
racers has acted suspiciously.

00:04:44.994 --> 00:04:49.248
You have to take part in the race,
or you can't get the prize.

00:04:49.331 --> 00:04:52.585
So the culprit has to be one of these guys.

00:04:52.668 --> 00:04:56.422
But since no one has raised any suspicions...

00:04:56.505 --> 00:04:59.925
There has to be an outside accomplice.

00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:05.264
It's possible that an accomplice
is sabotaging things remotely.

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:09.101
Please check the EM wave
transmission records at once.

00:05:17.651 --> 00:05:20.237
So then, that goes for the last explosion, too.

00:05:20.321 --> 00:05:22.907
This is the work of someone
who is trying to get the feather.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.911
The bastard! Just which
contestant is the culprit?!

00:05:26.994 --> 00:05:31.916
| still don't know. But the culprit
isn't necessarily a contestant.

00:05:31.999 --> 00:05:34.585
That was my thinking when I installed this.

00:05:34.668 --> 00:05:38.297
So that's why, is it? Doggie, you're smart.

00:05:40.341 --> 00:05:42.259
We've found the source of the transmissions!

00:05:42.343 --> 00:05:44.803
But how do we get there?

00:05:52.353 --> 00:05:55.606
We will take you to the medical tent at once.

00:05:55.689 --> 00:05:58.943
Excuse me, but we'd like to go somewhere else.

00:05:59.026 --> 00:06:00.569
Huh?

00:06:00.653 --> 00:06:02.780
If you please.

00:06:09.995 --> 00:06:14.250
The Ryobi, which got hung up at
the third checkpoint, is catching up!

00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:16.585
Moving up into the sky
above would make this easier,

00:06:16.669 --> 00:06:19.255
but that would be a risky gamble!
The reason being,

00:06:19.338 --> 00:06:23.592
above these ravines are particle
beam guns, equipped with sensors,

00:06:23.676 --> 00:06:27.596
and if you rise above a set
altitude, you will be shot at!

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.932
Of course, the beams are
set at their lowest level,

00:06:30.015 --> 00:06:32.810
and there is no danger to the racers.

00:06:36.355 --> 00:06:39.358
Knowing the risks, the Ryobi takes its chances!

00:06:43.654 --> 00:06:47.116
Unfortunately, the Ryobi
drops out at this point!

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:51.245
What is the matter?

00:06:51.328 --> 00:06:54.582
Kuro-pon says he wants
to speak to you, Tomoyo-chan.

00:06:54.665 --> 00:06:57.293
It's about time you told us the truth.

00:07:04.341 --> 00:07:05.634
Tell us.

00:07:07.011 --> 00:07:09.930
| am the one who manipulated the race.

00:07:10.014 --> 00:07:12.600
Oh, is that right?

00:07:12.683 --> 00:07:16.937
Which is to say, I only
tampered with the preliminary race.

00:07:17.021 --> 00:07:20.941
| scattered the nanomachines
into the race track airspace.

00:07:21.025 --> 00:07:22.943
Why would you do such a thing?

00:07:23.027 --> 00:07:25.237
| did it...

00:07:25.321 --> 00:07:29.450
...in order to return
Sakura-chan's feather to her.

00:07:36.665 --> 00:07:40.586
A year ago, now, my company's
excavations team discovered

00:07:40.669 --> 00:07:45.799
an unusual energy source, in the
shape of a feather, beneath the sea.

00:07:47.343 --> 00:07:50.929
Shortly after that, I was
told by a certain person

00:07:51.013 --> 00:07:54.266
that the feather belonged to Sakura-chan.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:59.313
But that was after we had gone
public with news about the feather.

00:08:00.689 --> 00:08:04.276
The unusual feather became an object
of attention throughout the land,

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.904
to say nothing of neighboring lands.

00:08:06.987 --> 00:08:10.574
As large-scale an enterprise as
the Piffle Princess Company may be,

00:08:10.658 --> 00:08:13.911
they still could not turn over a feather
that had gathered the attention

00:08:13.994 --> 00:08:17.247
of the world without
explaining the reasons why.

00:08:17.331 --> 00:08:21.919
And so, I made it the prize in this race.

00:08:22.002 --> 00:08:26.256
By making it the race prize, they could
turn it over without making waves.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:30.928
What's more, it makes it possible to
smoke out the ones who are after it.

00:08:31.011 --> 00:08:35.265
However, it also meant
exposing you all to danger.

00:08:35.349 --> 00:08:38.602
And so, we are the ones who
rigged things in the preliminary race

00:08:38.686 --> 00:08:40.270
to make it look like there was cheating,

00:08:40.354 --> 00:08:42.940
and had everyone increase their wariness.

00:08:43.023 --> 00:08:48.904
So that's it. Or so I'd like to say,
but what if we didn't win the race?

00:08:48.987 --> 00:08:51.573
| was not worried about that.

00:08:51.657 --> 00:08:56.245
This certain person said that |
could place my faith in your strength.

00:08:56.328 --> 00:09:00.916
| don't understand this! You keep
mentioning this "certain person."

00:09:00.999 --> 00:09:02.960
Just who is it?!

00:09:04.002 --> 00:09:06.255
We've discovered
the source of the transmissions.

00:09:06.338 --> 00:09:07.589
Where is it?

00:09:07.673 --> 00:09:09.133
The thing is...

00:09:10.342 --> 00:09:12.052
From my company?!

00:09:20.352 --> 00:09:23.105
To think that the culprit is
in the Piffle Princess Company,

00:09:23.188 --> 00:09:24.940
which is sponsoring the race!

00:09:25.023 --> 00:09:30.237
Wreck the sanctity of a race, will you?!
Just you watch what I do to you!

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.240
Once this ravine is cleared,
the goal will be right in front of them!

00:09:33.323 --> 00:09:37.911
Will victory go to the Snow White?
Or will it go to the Spirit?

00:09:37.995 --> 00:09:41.915
Oh, the Wing Egg is
frantically closing the gap!

00:09:41.999 --> 00:09:45.794
The Wing Egg has finally
made its way to the top!

00:09:47.337 --> 00:09:51.592
My next target is the Wing Egg.

00:09:51.675 --> 00:09:53.469
Very well.

00:10:12.988 --> 00:10:18.452
Target lock-on.
Commencing particle beam power charge.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:24.917
Wing Egg, say your prayers.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.293
Stop!

00:10:29.338 --> 00:10:31.924
W-What's this? What's going on?

00:10:32.007 --> 00:10:33.634
You...

00:10:37.346 --> 00:10:40.140
He's the Piffle president's secretary.

00:10:50.025 --> 00:10:52.152
Eliminate the intruders.

00:10:56.323 --> 00:10:58.242
How do you like that? You can't move.

00:10:58.325 --> 00:11:02.579
You can watch on pensively from there,
as your friend meets her end.

00:11:02.663 --> 00:11:05.290
If I don't do something,
the Princess will be...

00:11:06.333 --> 00:11:08.293
Moko-chan, hold on!

00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:17.594
Let me take care of this.

00:11:17.678 --> 00:11:18.595
Huh?

00:11:18.679 --> 00:11:20.264
I'll draw its fire.

00:11:20.347 --> 00:11:21.932
But that's dangerous!

00:11:22.015 --> 00:11:24.977
| have to pay you back
for what you did earlier.

00:11:36.989 --> 00:11:37.948
What?!

00:11:43.662 --> 00:11:44.955
That's enough.

00:11:50.002 --> 00:11:51.336
Doggie!

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:58.051
Princess, it's up to you now.

00:12:09.354 --> 00:12:11.940
Where is the goal?

00:12:12.024 --> 00:12:12.941
Puu...

00:12:13.025 --> 00:12:15.319
If we don't hurry,
they're going to catch up!

00:12:17.696 --> 00:12:18.989
The wind...

00:12:22.659 --> 00:12:24.745
Moko-chan, hold on!

00:12:35.672 --> 00:12:37.925
Goal!I

00:12:38.008 --> 00:12:42.638
In its first appearance,
the Wing Egg has attained victory!

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.975
Smooch! Smooch! A celebratory smooch!

00:12:48.018 --> 00:12:49.269
It's over?

00:12:49.353 --> 00:12:52.940
That's right. Sakura, you won!

00:12:53.023 --> 00:12:54.942
We won?

00:12:55.025 --> 00:12:56.944
Uh-huh!

00:12:57.027 --> 00:12:58.654
We did it!

00:13:01.323 --> 00:13:04.076
Whoo! That's our Sakura-chan!

00:13:04.159 --> 00:13:06.244
Kuro-pon, let's cheer for her together.

00:13:06.328 --> 00:13:07.913
As if.

00:13:07.996 --> 00:13:09.957
Come on, come on.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.920
You were hiding this so
Sakura-chan wouldn't worry, right?

00:13:15.003 --> 00:13:18.256
Kuro-sama, you're so cool for
doing that, so whoo, whoo with me.

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.634
Would you stop it with the "whoo"!

00:13:22.594 --> 00:13:28.809
Impressive, Sakura-chan. This is
proof positive that the feather is yours.

00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:37.943
That girl sure is amazing, huh?

00:13:38.026 --> 00:13:41.530
Mm-hmm, she really is amazing.

00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:44.574
But this isn't over yet.

00:13:46.994 --> 00:13:48.870
There is still...

00:13:49.997 --> 00:13:51.873
...one more culprit.

00:13:56.336 --> 00:13:59.881
And so, we will now
have the awards ceremony!

00:14:01.008 --> 00:14:02.926
The winner of the Dragonfly Race,

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:06.930
looking prettier and soaring
faster than anyone else,

00:14:07.014 --> 00:14:10.851
the pilot of the Wing Egg, Contestant Sakura!

00:14:20.694 --> 00:14:21.945
Mekyol!

00:14:22.029 --> 00:14:24.281
Congratulations.

00:14:24.364 --> 00:14:25.824
Thank you.

00:14:30.662 --> 00:14:32.289
You guys are close, huh?

00:14:39.671 --> 00:14:40.964
Princess!

00:14:43.675 --> 00:14:44.968
Princess...

00:14:54.686 --> 00:14:56.605
So, you've come after all.

00:14:56.688 --> 00:14:57.814
Get down!

00:14:59.357 --> 00:15:00.817
Why, that bastard...

00:15:03.028 --> 00:15:04.279
Ryuo!

00:15:04.362 --> 00:15:08.241
Don't worry about me...

00:15:08.325 --> 00:15:12.579
They are shock beams. He has
just been knocked out temporarily.

00:15:12.662 --> 00:15:14.247
Tomoyo-chan...

00:15:14.331 --> 00:15:17.125
Hurry, Sakura-chan,
take the feather inside you!

00:15:18.335 --> 00:15:20.962
Tomoyo-chan, how do you know about that?

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.770
So you are the other culprit, are you?

00:15:36.853 --> 00:15:38.980
That feather belongs to me.

00:15:41.691 --> 00:15:42.984
It's no use.

00:15:49.658 --> 00:15:50.575
What?

00:15:50.659 --> 00:15:52.577
Mokona, nice!

00:15:52.661 --> 00:15:55.580
That's one of Mokona's
108 secret techniques!

00:15:55.664 --> 00:15:58.583
Super-suction power!

00:15:58.667 --> 00:16:01.920
At this range, your shield won't work.

00:16:02.003 --> 00:16:04.256
The police will be here shortly.

00:16:04.339 --> 00:16:06.925
There's nowhere for you to run anymore.

00:16:07.008 --> 00:16:10.929
Come quietly, or you're going to get hurt.

00:16:11.012 --> 00:16:13.640
| seem to be quite out of luck.

00:16:16.351 --> 00:16:19.271
To think that I'd be stopped
by that strange creature,

00:16:19.354 --> 00:16:21.940
just like I was in Jade Country...

00:16:22.023 --> 00:16:24.943
I'm not a strange creature. I'm Mokona!

00:16:25.026 --> 00:16:28.280
Just a minute.
He just said "Jade Country," didn't he?

00:16:28.363 --> 00:16:29.948
Yeah.

00:16:30.031 --> 00:16:31.491
You don't mean...

00:16:40.667 --> 00:16:43.253
What made you suspect me?

00:16:43.336 --> 00:16:47.632
Then, you're the same
Dr. Kyle that was in Jade Country?

00:17:02.689 --> 00:17:07.944
In different worlds, there are other
people who have the same faces.

00:17:08.028 --> 00:17:12.991
However, there is no way to be
sure they really are different people.

00:17:15.327 --> 00:17:17.621
Remember that well.

00:17:30.675 --> 00:17:34.596
He vanished. Or rather,
he moved into another dimension.

00:17:34.679 --> 00:17:36.598
Yeah.

00:17:36.681 --> 00:17:40.268
Sure enough, it's just
like that person told me.

00:17:40.352 --> 00:17:44.606
I'd forgotten about that.
Hey, who is this person you're talking about?

00:17:44.689 --> 00:17:46.608
Princess Tomoyo.

00:17:46.691 --> 00:17:48.735
W-What did you say?!

00:17:50.362 --> 00:17:53.615
| will tell you everything.

00:17:53.698 --> 00:17:58.578
About that feather.
About the existence of other worlds.

00:17:58.662 --> 00:18:03.291
And about travelers
that will be coming in time.

00:18:04.334 --> 00:18:06.920
Who are you?

00:18:07.003 --> 00:18:10.257
| am you, from another world.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:15.929
We have the same face, and the same spirit,
but we live in different times.

00:18:16.012 --> 00:18:18.640
There is more than just one world.

00:18:22.018 --> 00:18:27.941
Please return the feather
to its owner, but be careful.

00:18:28.024 --> 00:18:32.779
There are those from other worlds
who are out to get the feather.

00:18:41.997 --> 00:18:45.250
The princess who appeared
in your dream said that?

00:18:45.333 --> 00:18:46.251
Yes.

00:18:46.334 --> 00:18:51.923
So you're saying that the two
of you tricked us, right?

00:18:52.007 --> 00:18:54.592
It was a whole lot of
trouble keeping up the act.

00:18:54.676 --> 00:18:57.595
I'm not very good at this.

00:18:57.679 --> 00:19:00.932
| was wracked with guilt
for having lied to a woman,

00:19:01.016 --> 00:19:02.934
and I thought my heart was going to burst.

00:19:03.018 --> 00:19:08.606
Still, I had no idea that
the accomplice was so close to me.

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.984
Thank you so very much.

00:19:13.361 --> 00:19:16.990
| must apologize to Sakura-chan, too.

00:19:44.351 --> 00:19:46.269
Does it hurt?

00:19:46.353 --> 00:19:47.312
Huh?

00:19:50.357 --> 00:19:52.275
Your left hand.

00:19:52.359 --> 00:19:54.319
It's nothing.

00:19:57.364 --> 00:19:58.990
In your dream...

00:20:00.033 --> 00:20:01.951
Nah, never mind.

00:20:02.035 --> 00:20:03.912
Something is bothering you.

00:20:03.995 --> 00:20:05.580
It's nothing.

00:20:05.663 --> 00:20:08.625
Please say whatever you have to say.

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:15.924
In your dream,
how was Princess Tomoyo doing?

00:20:16.007 --> 00:20:17.967
She was doing well.

00:20:19.344 --> 00:20:23.932
When she spoke of you,
she seemed to be very happy.

00:20:24.015 --> 00:20:26.935
She probably said all sorts
of ridiculous stuff about me.

00:20:27.018 --> 00:20:29.604
No, she said that knowing you,

00:20:29.687 --> 00:20:34.150
she was sure that you would
recognize what true strength was.

00:20:39.864 --> 00:20:43.326
Please get better soon,
without doing anything else rash.

00:20:44.994 --> 00:20:47.622
Your spirits are the same, huh?

00:21:12.021 --> 00:21:16.276
Doggie! Do you have to go?!

00:21:16.359 --> 00:21:20.655
Mm-hmm, but I'm sure we'll meet again.

00:21:22.031 --> 00:21:24.325
All right. Make sure we do.

00:21:27.996 --> 00:21:30.623
Mokona Modoki is all excited!

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:33.460
Puu!

00:21:36.671 --> 00:21:38.590
We had fun.

00:21:38.673 --> 00:21:40.258
Thank you very much.

00:21:40.341 --> 00:21:43.928
Tomoyo-chan, we'll see
each other again, right?

00:21:44.012 --> 00:21:46.931
Yes. We still do not have
the technology to cross dimensions

00:21:47.015 --> 00:21:51.603
in this land yet, but my company
will come up with it, just watch!

00:21:51.686 --> 00:21:54.981
So I am sure that we will see each other again.

00:22:00.862 --> 00:22:04.282
If you run into Princess Tomoyo in your dreams,

00:22:04.365 --> 00:22:07.619
tell her something for me.
“I'm coming back. Count on it."

00:22:07.702 --> 00:22:08.995
Okay.

00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:25.595
It appears that direct
intervention did not work, either.

00:22:25.678 --> 00:22:29.933
Or perhaps, it's best to say that
this would be the natural outcome.

00:22:30.016 --> 00:22:34.521
Are you planning to
send them to that place?

00:22:34.604 --> 00:22:39.943
| must see where it is
that the miracle leads to.

00:22:40.026 --> 00:22:43.321
Now, dump them into that land.

00:23:11.683 --> 00:23:18.982
You haven't yet realized

00:23:20.316 --> 00:23:28.908
that the two of us have the power
to change even yesterday

00:23:28.992 --> 00:23:33.246
For no reason, I'm lonely (lonely)

00:23:33.329 --> 00:23:37.917
With tears streaming down my face

00:23:38.001 --> 00:23:41.588
I'm missing my one and only (only)

00:23:41.671 --> 00:23:49.137
The one I trace out in the sky, and that's you

00:23:50.013 --> 00:23:55.268
Take my, take my hand,
and let's go on together,

00:23:55.351 --> 00:23:59.564
reach out, reach out your hand,
and catch hold of the wind,

00:23:59.647 --> 00:24:03.901
take my, take my hand,
and do not be afraid,

00:24:03.985 --> 00:24:11.576
hold my, hold my hand, and I can fly,

00:24:11.659 --> 00:24:16.748
when I'm with you

00:24:32.680 --> 00:24:33.306
Puu!

00:24:33.348 --> 00:24:35.600
Hey, listen to this! Kuro-pon is so awful!

00:24:35.683 --> 00:24:38.269
He tells me that if I know that
there's another feather in a world

00:24:38.353 --> 00:24:42.607
that we've already been to, to realize
it when we're there the first time!

00:24:42.690 --> 00:24:46.611
Puu, it's so aggravating!
I'm going to tell Yuko on him!

00:24:46.694 --> 00:24:49.947
Which land is it that Syaoran
and the others have visited already?

00:24:50.031 --> 00:24:52.283
Just wait until you see!

00:24:52.367 --> 00:24:54.952
Tsubasa Chronicles, "Sorrowful Miracle."

00:24:55.036 --> 00:24:57.997
Next time, your heart will
pound over the broken glass!
